---
const githubUrl = 'https://github.com/ArmandoHerra/pdf-toolkit';
---

<section class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <div
    class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_50%_-10%,rgba(244,63,94,0.20),transparent_60%)]"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
  </div>

  <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-28 text-center sm:py-36">
    <p class="mb-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-surface-800 bg-surface-800/60 px-4 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary-400">
      pypdf · pdfium · pikepdf · reportlab · pdfplumber — nothing AGPL or GPL
    </p>

    <h1 class="text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-surface-50 sm:text-6xl">
      pdf-toolkit
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-2xl font-semibold text-primary-400 sm:text-3xl">
      Every common PDF chore. One safe CLI. No copyleft underneath.
    </p>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-surface-100">
      One command-line tool for merge, split, extract, rotate, PDF↔images, text, tables,
      compress, encrypt, metadata, watermark, OCR and Office→PDF — orchestrating a
      permissively licensed engine stack behind one safe, scriptable interface.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 sm:flex-row">
      <a
        href="#quickstart"
        class="w-full rounded-lg bg-primary-500 px-7 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 shadow-lg shadow-primary-900/50 transition hover:bg-primary-400 sm:w-auto"
      >
        Get Started &rarr;
      </a>
      <a
        href={githubUrl}
        class="w-full rounded-lg border border-surface-800 px-7 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-surface-50 transition hover:border-primary-400 hover:text-primary-400 sm:w-auto"
      >
        View on GitHub &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
